id: pm-vcs-tj07
title: Include CDC benchmark source in the 100/100/100/100 coverage contract
description: "The pm-vcs coverage script explicitly excludes scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts. The full release gate is green and measures 39 source files, while the docstring gate sees 40; the benchmark is executable authored TypeScript and therefore the package cannot claim all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage under the current fleet requirement."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T13:15:34.304Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T06:59:53.495Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every authored executable TypeScript source file and reconcile the coverage and docstring scopes; include scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts or refactor its executable logic into measured source with real deterministic benchmark acceptance; measure statements, lines, branches and functions at 100% with no excludes, threshold reductions, skips or synthetic-only assertion; run the full release gate and real benchmark on the exact pushed head, then update the coverage evidence and PM links."
expected_result: "Every executable authored TypeScript source is measured at 100% across statements, lines, branches and functions, and the benchmark still runs against real file/object-store I/O."
actual_result: The c8 invocation uses --exclude=scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts. Its LCOV lists 39 source files at 100% lines/branches/functions; docstring gate reports 40 source files. The benchmark script is not part of the measured gate.
affected_version: 2026.7.30
component: quality
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T06:59:53.495Z",codex-sol,"Removed the coverage exclusion for scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts without changing the 100 percent thresholds. Added real full-benchmark execution plus empty-store and directory-noise boundary fixtures. Focused c8 reports 100 statements, branches, functions and lines for HTTP protocol, HTTP client, server and CDC benchmark; full all-source coverage is running. eslint, jscpd and the 239-declaration docstring gate pass."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T13:16:01.214Z",codex,"At current code head 21e8ed1, direct npm run release:check passed, including c8 --all --100, real native TOON/stat-cache/self-host acceptance, zero production audit and changelog check. The measured LCOV has 39 sources and 16030/16030 lines, 3351/3351 branches, 468/468 functions; scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts is explicitly excluded. This issue records the all-executable-source coverage gap without overstating those percentages."
  "2026-09-29T13:24:20.991Z",codex,"The real CDC benchmark completed on a temporary object store: for the declared 256 KiB corpus and 64-byte front insertion, object-count reuse was 95.00% with CDC default and 0.00% with fixed 4K; middle/end and throughput rows also emitted. Fresh npm and Bun packed projects with CLI 2026.9.29 committed a real file through pm-vcs and passed strict health. Neither result measures scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts under c8, so this issue remains open."
files[3]:
  - path: package.json
    scope: project
    note: Current c8 scope and explicit benchmark exclusion
  - path: scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts
    scope: project
    note: Executable authored benchmark source outside coverage scope
  - path: test/cdc-benchmark.test.ts
    scope: project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  node --test test/cdc-benchmark.test.ts,project,codex-sol,"2026-10-05T06:54:38.814Z",local_mutation,feat/served-repository-http
docs[2]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/79",global,Current package certification candidate carrying this owner issue
  .agents/pm/features/pm-vcs-lrdt.toon,project,Prior feature decision that accepted the benchmark exclusion
body: ""
